When the parametric method is used the function <math>\text{E}</math> takes the form

{{block center|<math>\left(\lambda\frac{\partial f}{\partial\dot{x}}+\mu\frac{\partial f}{\partial\dot{y}}\right)_{\dot{x}=\lambda,\ \dot{y}=\mu}-\left(\lambda\frac{\partial f}{\partial\dot{x}}+\mu\frac{\partial f}{\partial\dot{y}}\right)_{\dot{x}=l,\ \dot{y}=m}</math>}}

where <math>\lambda</math>, <math>\mu</math> are the direction cosines of the tangent at <math>\text{P}</math> to the curve <math>\text{AQPB}</math>, in the sense from <math>\text{A}</math> to <math>\text{B}</math>, and <math>l</math>, <math>m</math> are the direction cosines of the tangent at <math>\text{P}</math> to the stationary curve <math>\text{A}'\text{P}</math>, in the sense from <math>\text{A}'</math> to <math>\text{P}</math>.

